 ],
 "title": "GIDEON's Funding and Research on Malassezia pachydermatis",
 "summary": "GIDEON, a method or tool, is funded by the National Institute of General Medical Sciences and identifies BPMs, which in turn identifies LocalCut and Liany-ILP. GIDEON outperforms both Liany-ILP and LocalCut. Malassezia pachydermatis, an organism, has susceptibility to Miconazole and virulence to ergosterol. It is treated with ketoconazole and has upregulation of several genes, including ERG11, ERG24, ERG25, ERG3, and ERG5. These genes upregulate KTZ, a chemical. Miconazole, ketoconazole, and itraconazole are targets for lanosterol 14α-demethylase, a gene or protein.",
